    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.85) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from highly favorable matchups against back-end starters. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is our premier start, boasting a +19% SP skill advantage against Quantrill, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a strong +14% platoon edge and the friendly hitting environment against Young. Despite the scarcity of speed, **Nasim Nunez** (71.50) emerges as a vital inclusion; his elevated efficiency score is driven by a massive +18% matchup advantage against Young, proving that even lower-order hitters can provide elite value when the opposing arm is sufficiently exploitable.\n\nWhile **Sam Antonacci** (61.12) and **Kyle Tucker** (60.95) provide reliable, high-floor contributions, the most difficult personnel decision involved **Nolan Schanuel**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 51.72 score. Although **Nolan Schanuel** projects well, he ultimately fell behind the aggressive platoon-driven upside of **Josh Lowe** and the situational utility of our primary infielders. Owners should exercise caution with **Jackson Merrill** (53.44) and **Gunnar Henderson** (59.96) today; both face elite or near-elite arms in Yamamoto and Griffin respectively. While **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start due to his profile, the SP skill penalty applied to **Jackson Merrill** serves as a warning that his path to production is significantly harder than his season average suggests.",
